\title{Recurrences}
\date{2026-03-13T20:46:23Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{When we define a [sequence](00B1) via a formula for #{a_n} in terms of #{n}, we say it is in \em{closed form}. Another way to define a sequence is via a \em{recurrence}.}

